{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956644-are-boosted-spirits-rather-overpowered-in-a-fight","id":956644,"title":"Are \"boosted\" spirits rather overpowered in a fight?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-23T17:25:06-07:00","id":956644,"title":"Are \"boosted\" spirits rather overpowered in a fight?","content":"This covers many of the games since they all use the same mechanic. All spirits, ghosts, Angels and essence users can &quot;boost&quot;. Their traits by rank+2 in one round by spending essence? Is it just me or is this really powerful and makes regular spirits able to lay waste to an entire group of humans and/or supernaturals. A rank 2 spirit with a dice pool of 10 ( say 6 and 4 in power and finesse) with a defence of 4 can suddenly get a dice pool of 18 with a defence of 8. That could mean it's blows are devastating and any attack on it may be a chance die. And this is more extreme with Spirits rank 3 to 5. I see Werewolves being able to take down big spirits with pack tactics and the war form, but what about demons against a powerful angel or just a bunch of regular humans trying to take down a spirit or angel? Am I misreading the rules or is this how it was intended?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T17:36:49-07:00","id":956649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/956644-are-boosted-spirits-rather-overpowered-in-a-fight#post956644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A rank 2 spirit with a dice pool of 10 ( say 6 and 4 in power and finesse) with a defence of 4 can suddenly get a dice pool of 18 with a defence of 8.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, not exactly suddenly, it would take three turns to do. It wouldn't be able to get all that, either, as it costs 1 Essence per +1 and you're spending 12 Essence. You 'spend Essence to boost traits for a single scene on a point per dot basis,' and 'boosting takes a turn, and they can only boost a single Attribute in a turn.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That could mean it's blows are devastating and any attack on it may be a chance die. And this is more extreme with Spirits rank 3 to 5. I see Werewolves being able to take down big spirits with pack tactics and the war form, but what about demons against a powerful angel or just a bunch of regular humans trying to take down a spirit or angel? Am I misreading the rules or is this how it was intended? </div> </div> </div>I think you misread a little of the rules, as noted above, but the danger is real. Ephemerals are meant to be dangerous foes, even at low Rank, and a fight against a 'powerful angel' is likely to be part of a climax, or a hint from Storytellers that the characters, if they are not ready, better come back sometime when they are. Rank 3 beings are mighty on their own, certainly able to put an entire party in danger, and once you get to Rank 6 merely existing in the world can cause it to buckle and shudder under your metaphysical weight. The exponential growth in power of ephemeral ranks aren't equivalent to the linear progression of player Power Attributes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T09:44:20-07:00","id":957020,"title":"","content":"What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> said. It takes an ungodly amount of essence, it's slow, and not every spirit will have their reserves replete. I usually throw a d10 for every 2 ranks counting the first. Rank 1 spirits get a d10, same as rank 2; rank 3 and 4 get 2d10, rank 5 spirits get 3d10, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T09:54:22-07:00","id":957024,"title":"","content":"Well, if you see a Spirit going &quot;THIS ISN'T EVEN MY FINAL FORM&quot; for 3 turns and you don't run away or punch it really hard, you better be a powerhouse yourself. Otherwise, *run*.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}